 i also recognize that when we  did our animal crossing  tours which i planned and produced those  videos as well  people really liked the wholesome nature  of it so i was like okay let's  like expand on that keep these videos  funny and silly with obviously like ryan  reading people's favorite games but also  have different fun house members like  enthusiastically talking about their  favorite thing because people like to  see that kind of wholesome content so  yeah that is uh uh currently another  recurring series that i'm doing there  ben w said any plans to invite guests  from your troy austin or mike's  respective corners of the game industry  on future episode of play was justin  bieber [ __ ] that sentence up loving the  podcast so far oh thank you ben  uh look we've discussed this and it may  happen in the future  but the truth is that podcast came  together not because i picked a random  voice actor and a random composer and a  random director  um i certainly did you know pitch it to  them as that being the hook  but it's those four people because those  four people have such good chemistry  we really respect each other have solid  diversity of opinion  disagree with each other frequently so  it's very much about the conversation  flowing in the way that it does because  of those four people  um who obviously can also speak to their  various vocations and do in a very  informed  and i think passionate way but it's  entirely possible that if you removed  one of those pieces and added someone  else in  the show would feel completely different  so i'm hesitant to do it because the  chemistry is the selling point  and i really love that about the show um  but i can imagine if like  someone absolutely can't do one week  that we would have a guest on instead  josh keaton fan said why are you no  longer on inside gaming anymore  i get this question so frequently that  i've started to wonder if it's a meme  and that i'm just not in on the joke  i'm on inside gaming